{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1144019-falling-damage-logic","id":1144019,"title":"Falling damage logic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-26T04:19:50-07:00","id":1144019,"title":"Falling damage logic","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> According to both V20 and W20 the maximum damage a character receives from falling is 10 dices of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> This, basically, means a random human after falling from the top of a skyscraper will just stand up and walk away. 10 dices in average 5 success. Humans do not soak lethal, so 5 damage in, -2 modifier, walk to the hospital in their own.<br /> <br /> But what is more important, PCs are virtually immune to damage from falling and this harms the spirit of the game.<br /> Do you use any other system?<br /> I\u2019m considering 1 dice of damage per meter (3 feet) of fall. This is, approximately 3 dice of damage per floor.<br /> With a maximum of\u2026 30 dices of damage?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T07:07:32-07:00","id":1144049,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's a bit unrealistic for humans (and makes jumping from a skyscraper/plane to avoid a fight a viable tactic for some characters). I agree in that the damage should be higher (and if someone starts to point out the people who survived that kind of fall, with 30 dice you can still get 0-1 successes. Rather unlikely but so it's to fall from a plane and survive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T12:20:25-07:00","id":1144161,"title":"","content":"You could try using the vehicular ramming rules from Hunter's Hunted 2 or M20. Just remember to replace the vehicle size factor with something more appropriate to the size of the character falling.<br /> <br /> Also, an important thing to note is that terminal velocity will vary considerably for a shapeshifter. It can also become a moot point with the Gifts of Patagia or Spirit of the Bird, which allow for gliding and flight, respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T21:18:36-07:00","id":1144283,"title":"","content":"Another option is switching to the CofD method, which keeps the dice-pools from growing too large: The damage rating of a fall is automatic levels of damage plus dice of damage.<br /> <br /> You probably want to tweak the numbers a bit (10 max is probably too high for the WoD's usually set seven HLs), but it makes sure falls hurt while making them survivable (if much less reliably than the current rules).<br /> <br /> So if a terminal velocity fall is a 6L fall, it would do 6 lethal damage plus 6 dice of lethal damage. It's a bit more generous than reality, but it's still ~72% chance of outright death for a mortal without some way to mitigate the damage, ~15% chance of being incapacitated and laying there reliant on others to save you, and ~13% to limp away at 'just' taking 6 damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-27-2017, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T11:47:43-07:00","id":1144507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>erSito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1144019-falling-damage-logic#post1144019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what is more important, PCs are virtually immune to damage from falling and this harms the spirit of the game.<br /> Do you use any other system?<br /> I\u2019m considering 1 dice of damage per meter (3 feet) of fall. This is, approximately 3 dice of damage per floor.<br /> With a maximum of\u2026 30 dices of damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>The falling damage rules are horrid, really. Very horrid.<br /> But it is also tricky to make short, controlled falles statistically as harmless as they are in RL.<br /> <br /> That said, I think it is advisable to differentiate between two things: Controlled falls, and then uncontrolled falls - like tumbling off an edge, being shoved, etc. And of course, accidental messups on landing.<br /> <br /> I suggest the following:<br /> <br /> (For the sake of being complete with the measurement systems, 1 meter is roughly 3 feet)<br /> <br /> * Make it 1 dice per meter, bashing. And really, as an ST skip the roll for most 1 meter jumps by healthy people.<br /> * Roll Dex+athletics. Difficulty is the amount of meters * 2<br /> * On a failed roll, turn the damage dice into lethal. Still allow even mortals(!) to soak this damage.<br /> * On a botch on dex+ath, double the damage dice.<br /> * On an uncontrolled fall, raise difficulty by 2, double the damage dice. This stacks with above.<br /> * Surfaces softer than a hard floor remove damage dice. jagged, uneven surfaces increase them. ST decision.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> A controlled, 2 meter fall: 2 dice bashing. Easily soakable, and a 'safe' distance for somebody with good dex and athletics.<br /> Dex+athletics difficulty: 4<br /> An easy enough roll, but there is subtle potential for just landing wrong and getting an ouchie.<br /> <br /> However! If you are *shoved* over into a 2 meter fall or tumble over an edge, this is 4 dice, and dex+athletics is difficulty 6.<br /> The worst that can happen, is you get shoved or tumble, and *then* botch the dex+athletics - this would be 8 lethal. However, even mortals still can soak it.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Example 2:<br /> A controlled, 5 meter fall. 5 dice bashing. This is over two floors worth of jumping down. Not something anybody does easily.<br /> Dex+athletics difficulty: 10. That means difficulty 9 and 2 successes needed. Yes, there is a big potential for things to really hurt at this distance, even if you are a trained athlete.<br /> <br /> If you are *shoved*, it's 10 dice bashing, dex+athletics difficulty is 12. You need 3 succeses at difficulty 9 or this will seriously hurt. Do not botch. Spend a willpower.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This leaves room for good athletes, gifts, armor, magic et all to influence the odds involved. Especially for tough, athletic supernaturals. It also makes the danger scale quite up by distance - which is somewhat realistic.<br /> I am not sure what to cap the dice at.<br /> <br /> And for those who might consider these rules harsh:<br /> Landing from 5 meters is like being rammed at 34 km/h ( 22 miles per hour ) - by a planet sized wall that won't change course even a tiny bit from the fact. People have broken their backs from that height.<br /> <br /> The tricky thing is to make this allow for people to survive falls out of airplanes, but I think this covers normal situations quite well.<br /> <br /> <br /> .<br /> <br /> Bonus thought: Allow gifts that allow greater jumping distances also to influence the difficulty or damage dice here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-27-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T14:28:47-07:00","id":1144537,"title":"","content":"It feels like... well it's too much rules. Trying to be accurate with this is hard... but how much accuracy is really important here? How much system time do we really want to dedicate to &quot;I fell, how much damage do I take?&quot; esp. in a system that's not exactly high focused on accurate simulation?<br /> <br /> I mean, I really don't like the current RAW (or any of the previous editions for that matter), but let's face it. We're way more worried about extremely high falls not being 'scary' once people realize that jumping out of a plane probably isn't going to kill your PC before mundane traits or supernatural powers, than we're worried about falling off a ladder breaking a few bones on a nasty tumble. We don't want the game to get bogged down in the PCs constantly dealing realistically with everyday injuries, healing times, and long term issues that can persist after that.<br /> <br /> I mean, when we're escalating to thresholds this quickly (esp. given how thresholds interact with botches), the Dexterity + Athletics rolls is very quickly more, &quot;how badly do I fail?&quot; rather than, &quot;do I succeed or fail?&quot;<br /> <br /> It's also still getting into really high numbers on the potential damage. You need to be around 20 dice of lethal damage if something can soak it if you want it play out as deadly. Botching a 5m fall sounds bad in your system, but with soaking, most normal humans are looking at 3-4 final damage. That's a lot of math and rolls to get right back to where the original issue is.<br /> <br /> That's why I brought up the CofD method here. Some automatic damage lets you avoid the dice pool getting really high. There's also plenty of places for widgets to interact. You can still play with damage type, some things can reduce the automatic damage while others reduce the rolled damage, etc. You can also do what's been done with fire and sunlight damage where the soak difficulty is variable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T20:52:01-07:00","id":1144619,"title":"","content":"Oh, I agree that it adds some complexity to the rules - but it's less complexity in normal situations than the writeup might suggest.<br /> Essentially for normal falls, all you get is X dice per X meters, except for that additional dex+athletics check to see if the jumper does not mess up.<br /> <br /> Heck, amusingly enough, reading the normal 2nd edition CofD rules it seems they also pretty much go '1 auto damage for 3 meters', with the option of an dex+athletics roll to soften the blow if it's possible to hold on to something or to direct the fall onto a softer surface. I am not sure where you are getting the mixture of Auto X damage + damage dice from, (though it sounds interesting, mind).<br /> <br /> I simply don't like that the default rules' low damage levels (Even of the CofD rules), and that both old and new make absolutely no difference between &quot;hey, let's jump down here for fun / escape / training' and somebody deciding to shove you uncontrolled out of the window all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> If you want to simplyfy my system a bit along your lines, just make it '1 auto damage per 2 meters / 1 auto damage per meter if shoved', which would be the same thing statistically as my post's writeup. Dex+ath with according difficulty as above, then soak accordingly. So, two rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-27-2017, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T04:00:10-07:00","id":1144692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1144019-falling-damage-logic?p=1144619#post1144619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I agree that it adds some complexity to the rules - but it's less complexity in normal situations than the writeup might suggest.<br /> Essentially for normal falls, all you get is X dice per X meters, except for that additional dex+athletics check to see if the jumper does not mess up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how 'normal falls' is different than any falls. You math is always X dice per X meters except possibly doubling on a botched roll that could happen on any kind of fall.<br /> <br /> It's the issue of having to roll Dex + Ath every fall to see if you mess up and if so how badly that's the extraneous part to me. It's not &quot;roll to see if you succeed in reducing the impact of the fall,&quot; it's &quot;roll to see if you fuck up,&quot; which seems extraneous to me. If success doesn't do anything, why I am rolling?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (though it sounds interesting, mind). </div> </div> </div>Bah, House rule so old I forgot it is one. It's from the CofD 1e explosive rules (or the CofD 2e ones, but they did that in Hurt Locker with the numbers not linked like 1e did in Armory).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I simply don't like that the default rules' low damage levels (Even of the CofD rules), and that both old and new make absolutely no difference between &quot;hey, let's jump down here for fun / escape / training' and somebody deciding to shove you uncontrolled out of the window all of a sudden. </div> </div> </div>Aren't we all in agreement with the basic issue of the rules for falling being ridiculously generous?<br /> <br /> The problem is that being shoved only really matters over a relatively short fall (aka enough time to recover from the shock of it to fall correctly), and even then it's not that hard.to train to fall well despite that shock (I haven't done training for falls in over a decade, but I still use techniques without thinking about it when I slip, since that's the whole point of training on something for hours a week for years). I just don't think the system is granular enough for that. The difference in a short fall is not really controlled or not, but initial body position. If you're falling 5m, the biggest deal is what body part is pointed down when you start. A &quot;controlled&quot; drop on your head is going to be horrible for you, where an accidental fall on your feet is going to be far less painful. <br /> <br /> Why would controlled start or not even matter for a 20m or more fall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:47:02-07:00","id":1144971,"title":"","content":"Falling damage can easily be solved by just adding an absurd amount of bashing dice. I'd say a die for every foot beyond the first 10 feet. By the time you fall 30 feet, a survivable but bone breaking inducing fall, you'll be in pain but most likely not dead. Dex + Athletics roll to reduce the damage levels per success because rolling should do something.<br /> <br /> I do think vampires should really be able to survive the fall damage though; they really don't make them scary enough and the notion that a vampire dying because he got pushed out the window by some desperate or genius hunter would ruin all sense of threat from a vampire to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}